## Required phase order

1. Root first starts the real normal Host, uses the real CLI `init`/bootstrap path to create the isolated project and DRAFT goal, then closes that Host so the exclusive data-root lease is free. The existing CLI config must reference the target project and authorized workspace; the workspace must be exactly `<data_root>/workspace` under the repository `.local` tree and contain **only** the pinned regular `evidence.txt`; the old read-only vault must not overlap the new data root. Fill a new immutable copy of `seed.template.json` with actual absolute paths, IDs, SHA-256 and byte count. The initial discovery must carry the same Host ID/data root. The profile template must be pinned and contain the real model config/endpoint/route; no bearer material.
2. Root builds this changed revision from the Main module root using **four absolute named Go files**, with one owned Job and exact source pins. The command shape is `go build -trimpath -o <Root-owned-absolute-output.exe> "D:/作品集/ResearchOS/research-os/execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/mu_sdk_trusted_qualification_host_source_revision_codex/797a5659dec64d55a16915d1aea6e46c/main.go" "D:/作品集/ResearchOS/research-os/execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/mu_sdk_trusted_qualification_host_source_revision_codex/797a5659dec64d55a16915d1aea6e46c/hostapi.go" "D:/作品集/ResearchOS/research-os/execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/mu_sdk_trusted_qualification_host_source_revision_codex/797a5659dec64d55a16915d1aea6e46c/prepare.go" "D:/作品集/ResearchOS/research-os/execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/mu_sdk_trusted_qualification_host_source_revision_codex/797a5659dec64d55a16915d1aea6e46c/execute.go"`. The package-path build under `execution/v2.4` is invalid because that subtree is a separate module. Root may use a separately reviewed `.local` copy instead; neither path changes `go.mod`. Formatting or compile fixes must become another reviewed Source revision.
3. Run `--phase prepare --seed <pinned-seed.json> --receipt <new-prepare-receipt.json>` after CLI init and before the 300-second Root trial starts. After acquiring the data-root lease, it checks that no prior prepare state exists, then creates only a separate same-project ACTIVE qualification Goal/Task/profile/runtime/principals/frozen plan. It preserves the CLI target DRAFT goal and does not create AVAILABLE, PASS or provider effects. Its private state goes to `<data_root>/host/trusted-qualification-state.json`; Root should pin the public receipt and state hash/bytes but never print the private lease token.
4. Root freezes its whole-trial `started_utc` **before** the next phase. Run `--phase admit-only --seed <same-seed.json> --started-utc <RFC3339Nano-Z> --receipt <new-admit-receipt.json>`. This calls trusted OWNER `BeginRuntimeQualification` once and saves the real Run ID, epoch, created_at and lease token in private state. It checks a PREPARED, unstarted native dispatch and exits without `RunAdmitted` or a provider call. A crash/failure after `ADMIT_CLAIMED` is not auto-retried.
5. Root must start the helper as a suspended/owned Windows Job child with an open stdin pipe, under the same `started_utc+300s` deadline. Run `--phase execute-admitted --seed <same-seed.json> --ready-receipt <new-ready-receipt.json> --receipt <new-terminal-receipt.json>`. The helper binds actual loopback HTTP and native pipe, writes a private coordinator JSON and actual discovery (`url`, PID, data root, Host ID), then writes `READY_ADMISSION_PENDING`. It has still made **zero provider requests**. Root can now pin those actual files and the real qualification IDs into v8 basis and independent observer authority. The old CLI process must already be stopped; CLI ordinary work later uses the rewritten real discovery path.
6. Root creates and independently reviews a frozen GO authority JSON using `go.authority.template.json`, seven exact file pins, and the four supporting JSON records below; it sends one newline-delimited stdin frame `{"go":true,"authority_file":"<absolute-frozen-authority.json>"}`. The helper checks exact READY/discovery/coordinator hashes, admitted Run ID/epoch/profile/Host PID/URL, Root grant, consumed once marker, owned Host Job contract/probe, and 300-second deadline. Each of the four supporting GO JSON records is decoded from the same byte buffer whose length and SHA-256 passed its pin. It then saves a local execute-once fence **before** `RunAdmitted`. No second GO or relaunch is supported. Native/HTTP failure leaves the once fence for review, not retry.
7. On a genuinely SETTLED qualification Run with result Artifact, the helper requests independent `DETERMINISTIC_SERVICE` VERIFIER acceptance over v1 HTTP, requires returned PASS, calls `/runtimes/{id}/qualify` with the real LOG receipt, and grants `mu_turn` purpose until the earlier of qualification validity and Root deadline. It checks that no ordinary READY Task is already queued, then switches the HTTP runtime handler to the coordinator, starts ordinary scanning, and writes `<ready-receipt-stem>.ordinary.json` with `READY_FOR_ORDINARY`. Root may make its two ordinary model requests through the real CLI while keeping stdin open. Closing stdin or hitting the deadline cancels the Host and its children; Root must observe the exact Job tree and reconcile all provider effects separately.

## Supporting GO record bodies

The pinned `root_grant` JSON must contain `{"schema":"researchos.mu-trial-root-go.v1","approved":true,"qualification_run_id":"<Run>","started_utc":"<Root-start>"}`. The pinned `once_marker` must contain `{"schema":"researchos.mu-trial-once.v1","qualification_run_id":"<Run>","state":"CONSUMED_FOR_HOST_GO"}`. The pinned `outer_job_contract` must contain `{"schema":"researchos.mu-trial-host-job.v1","host_pid":<actual PID>,"root_job_id":"<opaque Root Job identity>","deadline_utc":"<Root-start-plus-300s>"}`. The pinned `host_job_probe` must contain `{"schema":"researchos.mu-trial-host-job-probe.v1","host_pid":<actual PID>,"root_job_id":"<same Job identity>","in_job":true,"descendant_of_root":true}`. These are additional Root-owned evidence, not facts created by this Source. The helper also calls Windows `IsProcessInJob` for a local any-Job check; Root must prove the exact ancestry externally.

## Previous build evidence retained

- The immutable previous Source and its original handoff remain at `execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/mu_sdk_trusted_qualification_host_source_codex/991a41da6cb146d9a5fae91c438f6d07/HANDOFF.md` (`2dc049426d043a02dbbfb227147649b1d1878554bfdd14ed4708664b9ef1079d`, 7695 bytes). This revision does not overwrite it.
- Root's first package-path build failed before type checking: `execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/integration_codex/trusted-host-build-7c2f6e6f4b884f00930fa07e1b4e508d/failure-origin.687.original-tool-io.json` (`b4398793ed2dba06f947a19881eb7d42225a436aea84aac42aad771194e0ee19`, 3691 bytes), with original `compile.stderr.raw` (`586902b7c98d4260510ff4661cd79fac956b8fe01a0f99b26bad04af103d544d`, 212 bytes). Its error was `main module ... does not contain package .../execution/v2.4/...`.
- Root then built the **previous** four-file Source successfully using named files: `execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/integration_codex/trusted-host-named-file-build-1d640c13b19a49c5aeb1607aeae2c170/compile.closed.json` (`66aac6d373721806326d467e75584b35c2ec4b93d179cc786d122256fbf3a31f`, 1191 bytes), with `compile.invocation.json` (`91d4bba0bac29059e9d61ffbc69097a4b3935bdffc73fc838aa8a24dd1899777`, 4484 bytes). It reports zero target Host runs and zero provider calls. The changed revision here has no compile result.

## OPEN before Root execution

- Current Root controller callback owns one child only. It has not yet proven that the READY Host process, subsequent CLI and every Mu/provider child share the required whole-trial Job/deadline. Root needs a separately reviewed Host Job lifecycle or a new controller revision supporting multiple suspended children. The helper's `IsProcessInJob` check alone does not close this.
- The concrete seed/profile values, actual Node/bundle/vault pins, initial CLI project/DRAFT goal, isolated witness, Root GO grant, and independent observer authority are not supplied in this Source. Templates have placeholders and cannot run as-is.
- The new four Go files remain proposed bytes. Root must compile these exact new pins and independently review them; the previous build does not certify this revision. No new native pipe, model call, acceptance, or end-to-end 300-second run has executed.
- Seed profile, Node executable and bundle are read once and the verified in-memory bytes create the sealed profile. Later native subprocess launch still consumes the Node and bundle **paths**; their bytes could change between pin validation and launch. The Source does not close this runtime path TOCTOU; Root must provide an immutable path/identity fence or explicitly record it OPEN before GO.
- The Host tool policy is one read call, 4096 read bytes, zero write paths and 4096 write-byte ceiling, matching the intended v9 runner contract. This Source does not edit the runner. Root must separately close its current `{}` versus `[]` policy representation mismatch.
